{"kind":"stack","id":"stk-electric-appliances","title":"Appliances that run on electricity","theme":{"background":"#f4f9ff","foreground":"#1d2b3a","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Electricity"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"A form of energy that flows through wires and powers many machines in our homes."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Appliance"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"A machine in the home that does a job, such as cooking food or washing clothes."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"bulb"},{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these appliances needs electricity to work?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"A toaster","why":"A toaster heats bread using electrical current flowing through its wires.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"A wooden spoon","why":"A spoon is a simple tool with no motor or heating element.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"A cardboard box","why":"A box is a container and has no parts that need power.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What powers a washing machine when it spins?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Electricity","why":"The motor that turns the drum runs on electrical power from the plug.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Wind blowing in","why":"Pupils may think wind moves things, but washing machines have no wind inlet.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Sunlight","why":"Some solar panels use sunlight, but a washer is plugged into the mains.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Which appliance keeps food cold using electricity?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"A fridge","why":"A fridge uses an electric motor and compressor to keep food cool.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"A bread bin","why":"A bread bin keeps bread dry and has no cooling parts.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"A fruit bowl","why":"A bowl holds fruit but does not cool anything.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You arrive home and the power is out. Do you check the fuse box or light a candle?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Check the fuse box","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Light a candle","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You find a switch tripped and reset it. The lights come back on. Well done!"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"A candle gives light, but it is not electricity. Always use a torch and stay safe."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which of these is a common appliance that runs on electricity?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"A kettle","why":"A kettle heats water with an electric element, so it runs on electricity.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"A bicycle","why":"A bicycle is powered by pedalling, not by electricity.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"A football","why":"A football is kicked by hand and feet and needs no power.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"What does a television need to work?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Electricity","why":"A television uses electrical power to light its screen and play sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Water","why":"Water is not used to power a television.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Sand","why":"Sand is not used to power a television.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"You finished the electrical appliances lesson!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Great work. You now know how common appliances use electricity to help us at home."}],"actions":[]}}
